DTSTART:20261017T170000Z
DTEND:20261017T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
SUMMARY:CANCELLED-Discover the New Jersey Cranberry-CANCELLED
DESCRIPTION:About the program\n\nThere aren't many fruits that are native 
 to the United States. Cranberries are one of them. Before Europeans came\, 
 Native Americans used them for food\, medicine\, and dye. Since the 1800s\, 
 cranberries have been a big crop in New Jersey. This text discusses the 
 background\, significance\, and growing of these sour berries in New 
 Jersey. The text will also look at cranberry-based early American 
 recipes.\n\nAbout the presenter\n\nJudith Krall-Russo has consistently had 
 a passion for cuisine\, especially the plentiful farming in her home state 
 of New Jersey. She commenced her exploration of the customs and rituals 
 surrounding this prevalent beverage three decades ago and has subsequently 
 acquired qualifications as a tea expert from The Specialty Tea Institute of 
 New York and The Tea School in Pomfret\, Connecticut. She is likewise a 
 specialist and scholar in the field of tea. Krall-Russo is currently 
 engaged in the Gong Fu Chinese tea ceremony at The Tea Gallery and the 
 Japanese tea ceremony at the Uresenke Chanoyo Center in New York City.
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Lecture
UID:LibCal-10341-16814009
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16814009
END:VEVENT
