DTSTART:20261101T190000Z
DTEND:20261101T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20261101T000000Z
SUMMARY:From Swastika to Jim Crow (2000): Screening and Discussion
DESCRIPTION:Explore an influential\, little-known chapter in the history of 
 Black-Jewish relations in America. We'll be screening a documentary film\, 
 From Swastika to Jim Crow\,  based on a book by the same title by Gabrielle 
 Simon Edgcomb. It tells the story of German-Jewish refugees\, who\, 
 expelled from their homeland by Hitler and the Nazis\, found new lives and 
 careers at historically Black colleges and universities in the American 
 South\, influencing a whole generation of Black students and professionals. 
 After the screening\, Dr. Lillie Johnson Edwards and Rabbi Julie Roth\, 
 will discuss the film's significance. Dr. Edwards is a Drew University 
 Professor Emerita of History and African American Studies. Rabbi Roth leads 
 Congregation Shomrei Emunah of Montclair\, NJ.\n\nThis program is 
 co-sponsored by Shomrei Emunah (https://shomrei.org/) and The Mark 
 Montclair https://themarkmtc.org).
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
UID:LibCal-10306-17084521
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17084521
END:VEVENT
