X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ics Kstx8Swyw669Kakgqa 6478083 Ics": "https://teamup.com/kstx8swyw669kakgqa/events/2186006684"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ics_kstx8swyw669kakgqa_6478083_ics
SUMMARY:Midday Meetup - Estate Planning
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T141500
DTSTAMP:20261017T000314Z
UID:TU2186006684
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261111T123000
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261012T213850Z
DESCRIPTION:**Midday MeetUp**   \nA monthly gathering to make connections 
 and learn together.  \n12:30pm Catered Lunch (free)  \n1:15pm Featured Pro
 gram   \n  \n**Topic** - Estate Planning: Four documents. Two tax systems.
  One integrated plan.  \n**Presenter** - Linda F. Spiegel\, Esq   \n  \n**
 Cost:** FREE or Suggested Donation of $10 per person to offset costs. (Bil
 l My Account is only open to Shomrei Members)  \n  \n**RSVP:** Required so
  we know how much food to buy.  \nhttps://shomrei.easyshul.com/events/6ad0
 ffd03e7684002567f097  \n  \n**\\***Members should use their fob to access 
 the building.  \n  \n**About the Program**  \nJoin Linda F. Spiegel for an
  overview of four essential estate planning documents: three that protect 
 your wishes during your lifetime and one that guides the distribution of y
 our estate after death. Learn how New Jersey’s inheritance tax and the f
 ederal estate tax fit into one integrated plan for your future.  \n  \n**A
 bout the Speaker**  \nLinda F. Spiegel\, Esq.is an Elder Care Planning med
 iator and works with families to help them with issues arising from aging 
 relatives. When she is not mediating or arbitrating Ms. Spiegel works with
  individuals\, couples and families in estate planning. She is also a divo
 rce mediator assisting couples to reach an amicable resolution of their is
 sues.  \n  \nMs. Spiegel graduated from Barnard College\, Columbia Univers
 ity and the Boston University School of Law. She is the Chair of the Ameri
 can Bar Association’s Senior Lawyers Division Alternate Dispute Resoluti
 on (ADR) Committee. In January. she was inducted into the National Academy
  of Distinguished Neutrals and is a recipient of a Joint Resolution of the
  Senate and General Assembly of the State of New Jersey for her work as a 
 volunteer attorney with Project SARAH\, Stop Abusive Relationships at Home
 .  \n  \nAdditional_Dates_for_for_Midday_MeetUps: https://shomrei.org/cale
 ndar/midday-meetup-calendar  \n  \n**Questions?** Contact Office   \noffic
 e@shomrei.org   \n  \n\\#middaymeetup\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261016T214437Z
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL;VALUE=URI:https://teamup.com/kstx8swyw669kakgqa/events/2186006684
X-SOURCE:Congregation Shomrei Emunah
END:VEVENT
