 e of Israel. As the country found its footing\, these thinkers wrestled wi
 th questions that remain deeply relevant today: How “Jewish” should Is
 rael be? What obligations does a Jewish state have toward non-Jewish citiz
 ens? And what spiritual meaning\, if any\, do modern Israeli holidays like
  Yo
