DTSTART:20261206T190000Z
DTEND:20261206T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20261206T000000Z
SUMMARY:Folk & Blues with Tal Naccarato
DESCRIPTION:About the program\n\nA guitarist\, singer-songwriter\, and 
 musician in the Americana\, folk\, and blues styles plays solo acoustic 
 music from his original and traditional repertoire. He also talks about and 
 plays examples of the history of this style of music while showing off and 
 playing rare vintage instruments during a live concert.\n\n\n\nAbout the 
 artist\n\nTal Naccarato is a vibrant composer\, songwriter\, and teaching 
 artist whose roots stretch from the medieval mountain village of 
 Fiumefreddo\, Bruzio\, Italy\, to the vibrant community of East Flatbush\, 
 Brooklyn. His original music is a mix of folk\, Americana\, rock\, and 
 blues\, mixed with classical guitar elements and a distinct bluesy swing. 
 Tal was the first-place winner in the Long Island Blues Society Solo/Duo 
 Competition in 2023. He performs solo acoustic shows\, both with original 
 music and traditional songs. Everyone is welcome.
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10341-17690175
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17690175
END:VEVENT
