 New York Times bestselling author and illustrator of Cook Korean!: A Comic 
 Book with Recipes\, as well as the graphic novel memoir Almost American 
 Girl and historical fantasy graphic novel The Fox Maidens. Her comics and 
 illustrations have also appeared in various publications\, including The 
 Washington Post and The Los Angeles Times\, as well as in anthologies 
 highlighting Asian American culture: Rise: A Pop History of Asian America 
 from the Nineties to Now\, New Frontiers: The Many Worlds of George Takei\, 
 and Shattered: The Asian American Comics Anthology (Secret Identities). 
 Robin grew up reading and drawing comics. At fourteen she moved to the 
 United States from Seoul\, Korea. She studied illustration at Rhode Island 
 School of Design. She now lives in Virginia.\n\n\n\n
