DTEND:20261217T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261216T000000Z
SUMMARY:Laugh-Out-Loud Nostalgia: Bringing Junie B. Jones to Life in Comics with Colleen AF Venable
DESCRIPTION:Generations of readers grew up laughing with the world’s 
 funniest kid\, and now she’s back in a vibrant\, visual format! Join us 
 for a lively virtual conversation with National Book Award finalist Colleen 
 AF Venable as we explore her acclaimed comic adaptations in Junie B. Jones: 
 A Graphic Novel.\n\nBringing Barbara Park’s beloved\, spunky first-grader 
 into full-color comic panels\, Colleen captures all the energy\, humor\, 
 and heart of the original series for both nostalgic fans and a new 
 generation of readers. \n\nDiscover how Colleen translated Barbara Park's 
 beloved chapter books into dynamic graphic novel scripts while honoring the 
 original spirit\, and learn how text and comic art work together to bring 
 Junie B.'s hilarious expressions and schoolyard misadventures to 
 life.\n\nRegister today and discover how visual storytelling keeps classic 
 stories alive for readers of all ages!\n\n \n\nAbout the Author: 
 \n\nCOLLEEN AF (Ann Felicity) VENABLE is the author of many kids books\, 
 including the Katie the Catsitter series. Colleen discovered Junie B. as a 
 young babysitter and says\, "I don't think any character in literature 
 connects with me as much!"
LOCATION:Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Author Event/Talk
UID:LibCal-10286-17725384
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17725384
END:VEVENT
